     aaee — Attansic/Atheros L2 FastEthernet controller driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee mmiiiibbuuss
           ddeevviiccee aaee

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_ae_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aaee device driver provides support for Attansic/Atheros L2 PCIe
     FastEthernet controllers.

     The controller supports hardware Ethernet checksum processing, hardware
     VLAN tag stripping/insertion and an interrupt moderation mechanism.  At‐
     tansic L2 also features a 64-bit multicast hash filter.

     The aaee driver supports the following media types:

     aauuttoosseelleecctt   Enable autoselection of the media type and options.  The
                  user can manually override the autoselected mode by adding
                  media options to rc.conf(5).

     1100bbaasseeTT//UUTTPP  Select 10Mbps operation.

     110000bbaasseeTTXX    Set 100Mbps (FastEthernet) operation.

     The aaee driver provides support for the following media options:

     ffuullll--dduupplleexx  Force full duplex operation.

     hhaallff--dduupplleexx  Force half duplex operation.

     For more information on configuring this device, see ifconfig(8).

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The aaee driver supports Attansic/Atheros L2 PCIe FastEthernet controllers,
     and is known to support the following hardware:

     ••   ASUS EeePC 701
     ••   ASUS EeePC 900

     Other hardware may or may not work with this driver.

